experiment: phaseteach
  phaseteach -- can a taught utterance occupy two phases of the
  creature's own free-running F1 gesture?
  the quantity  produced F1 in phase 1 minus produced F1 in phase 0
  the evidence  the DIFFERENCE between the two mappings, because the
                oscillator contributes to both equally and cancels
  refused if    the two mappings come back equal, or ph_off is not ~0,
                or ph_share is near 0 or 1 (a settled winner, not an
                alternation, and one phase bin nearly empty)


  arm           n     F1 ph0    F1 ph1  separation (ph1-ph0)    share    off
  held          0          -         -  (one phase bin empty)    0.00   0.00
  phase        18      615.2     634.3  +19.1 +/- 0.1 Hz         0.50   0.00
  phase-sw     18      616.0     635.3  +19.3 +/- 0.2 Hz         0.50   0.00

  THE MAPPING CONTRAST, paired on seed (identity minus swapped)
    phase - phase-sw   -0.2 +/- 0.2 Hz  (0.8 SE, n=18)
  the identity mapping asks the HIGH-F1 posture for the LOW target and the
  swapped one asks it for the HIGH target, so a taught separation makes
  this NEGATIVE. The oscillator contributes equally to both and cancels.

  THE LESSON DOES NOT REACH THE PHASE. The two mappings are
  indistinguishable (-0.2 +/- 0.2 Hz, under 3 SE) at power to see a
  separation of 0.7 Hz, so the phase difference in the table is the
  OSCILLATOR and the reward has no purchase on it. The gesture runs and
  the lesson cannot aim it, which locates the gap at the COUPLING rather
  than at either part -- both of which are separately measured to work.
